Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:49:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Combine all table entry hashes of an item in the public
 API hash

`ReachabilityGraphHashes::add_node_hash` is called once for each metadata table entry of an item, but it replaced the item's hash with `hash.combine_commutative(hash)`, which ignores the hash so far. So only the last entry encoded for an item counted, and a change in any earlier entry did not change the public API hash. For example, with the items in a module file and edition 2024, changing the value of a `pub const` or a `pub static`, or a deprecation note, kept the hash, so a build system could skip compiling dependents that would see the new value.

Combine the new entry hash with the current one instead.

The new run-make test rewrites the source between compilations, because switching values with `cfg` attributes (as the incremental `rdr` tests do) changes the hash through the attributes alone. It fails without this change.
